<title>KAZAKHSTAN: World Bank withholds $180 mln loan for Uzbekistan.</title>
<headline>World Bank withholds $180 mln loan for Uzbekistan.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>An official with the World Bank said on Thursday it had withheld a $180 million loan earmarked for Uzbekistan's privatisation programme, citing foreign exchange constraints in the former Soviet republic.</p>
<p>&quot;The problem is that there are foreign exchange restraints which are not very conducive to privatisation,&quot; Hasso Molineus, World Bank representative in the Uzbek capital Tashkent, told Reuters by telephone.</p>
</text>
